+/*
+ * maple (4.4 kernel) adaptation: the kernel is configfs-only (no legacy
+ * f_adb gadget, no /dev/android_adb), so this file gains a FunctionFS
+ * transport backported from KitKat's adb (android-4.4.4_r2
+ * system/core/adb/usb_linux_client.c). Selection: FFS is used when
+ * /dev/usb-ffs/adb exists (created + mounted by init.maple.rc); otherwise
+ * the legacy /dev/android_adb path is kept for other devices. The gadget
+ * configfs skeleton and the UDC re-bind loop live in the device tree
+ * (init.maple.rc + usbudc.sh); adbd only writes its descriptors to ep0 and
+ * retries until the endpoints appear (usbudc may not have bound the UDC
+ * yet when adbd starts).
+ */
